      "message": "I can revert this, sure.\n\nMy intention here was to clarify the different steps of the dynamic layout generation; \"phase 1\" and \"phase 2\" don\u0027t really refer to anything within the logs and if you want to understand better what\u0027s going on, you have to delve into the code to realize \"phase 1\" includes dependent changes to config repos to validate the future global config; and \"phase 2\" doesn\u0027t include them and generates the actual config that will be applied to the buildset.\n\nMaybe this\u0027d deserve to appear in the docs as this doesn\u0027t seem to be covered: https://zuul-ci.org/docs/zuul/latest/search.html?q\u003dphase\u0026check_keywords\u003dyes\u0026area\u003ddefault - maybe a section about how Zuul computes a change\u0027s configuration.",
